# 252 · The rest of Setup: its first screen, Spend, Storage with Exports and Backup, Logs and System

**Status:** `READY` · **Version:** [v0.3.0](../roadmap.md#v030) · **Depends on:** [243](243-web-app-base.goal), [244](244-one-door.goal)

## What

A plan only; nothing of it is built. The design is the agreed mockup (goal [243](243-web-app-base.goal)). This is stage 6 of [the app's build plan](../app-build-plan.md#4-the-order). The area was "Usage, Logs and the rest of Settings". It is the rest of **Setup**, the place at the foot of the navigation: what Setup holds beside the models, agents, tools and access of goal [245](245-providers-and-set-up.goal) and the account of goal [261](261-sign-in-as-a-person.goal).

**The screens**

1. **Setup,** its first screen: one sentence that says whether everything works, and one table of Setup's parts: each part with what it holds under its name, and how it is now in one plain line. A row opens the part. One line is coloured, the one that is wrong.
2. **Spend:** what the models and the rented machines cost, over every run, for a time the owner picks. Its sentence says the cost and why; then four facts, with the calls for each day as a line; the use by campaign; each plan against its limit; the rented machines as one row; and one closed fold, By model. A row opens the campaign. A plan whose use cannot be read says so, with its one act. A budget is a row only when one is set. It takes the place of Metrics › Model use.
3. **Storage:** what Thermite keeps, where, and what removes it. Its sentence says how much and what removes it; then two facts, one table of the kinds, the largest first, and one closed fold with each machine's share. One button, **Add a rule**: a rule is today's retention policy. With a rule set, a block of rules stands above the table, one row a rule. Exports and Backup are two links. It takes the place of the pages on space, on retention policies and of Metrics › Storage.
4. **A rule's form** asks five things: its name, what it removes, where, the rule itself and when. The line beside **Save** says what the rule would remove now, before it is saved. As drawn, a saved rule is on, and Turn it off is in its menu (Open questions). Remove is done at once, with Undo: nothing but the rule is lost. Run it now asks once.
5. **Exports,** from Storage: every export Thermite keeps, the newest first: what was exported with one line on it, its kind, its size, when it was made. A row downloads it as one file. A search and one filter, the kind. A row's menu has Download, Details and Delete; Delete asks once, with the run's name typed. An export that is still arriving says so in its row (item 2 of goal [131](131-ux-fixes-found-in-use.goal)). A run's own export and a campaign's results are downloaded where the work is (goal [247](247-campaigns-and-runs.goal)).
6. **Backup,** from Storage: when Thermite was last backed up and whether the backup was whole, and two rows, to back up and to restore, each the command in short with **Copy**. The restore's steps are in the guide. A restore that Thermite refused is one line, with the link to the guide.
7. **Logs:** who changed what, the newest first: when, who, what they did in one sentence, on what. A burst of the same act is one row. One search and one filter, who. A row opens the entry beside the list: its sentence, four facts, and links to what it changed and to its raw fields. The second view is **Commands:** each thing Thermite asked a run or a machine to do, and how far it got. A command that hangs is the first row, with **Cancel it**. It takes the place of the audit log's page.
8. **System:** whether Thermite itself is well: its sentence; its parts as rows (the part, one line on what it does, one fact, its state as one word); its own resources, each with a line over time and its limit in words; one closed fold, Versions. A part's row opens the part, one level down: the server (its settings, its log level, its loops, its memory), the database (its largest tables), the message bus (its streams as one table, and from a stream its messages). A part that is down turns its row red, with the one thing to do. It takes the place of Metrics › Bus, Control and Rigs, and of the message bus's page.
9. **The other states** are on the board beside these: a rule set and a rule's menu; an export's menu and its deletion; a refused restore; Commands, with one that hangs; a log entry open; a part that is down; the message bus's streams.

**What it needs from control**

10. **There today:** cost by campaign and by model; the kinds of what is kept; rules with their preview, on and off, a run and their removals; an export's download and deletion; the commands and a command's cancel; the system's parts, the streams and their messages, and control's log level.
11. **Needs a read:**
    - One state line for each part of Setup.
    - On Spend: 30 days as a time, the calls by day, each plan against its limit, and a GPU cloud's bill.
    - Every export in one list. Today the read is rig by rig.
    - On Logs: the filter by who, the search, and a burst as one row.
    - Control's CPU, memory and disk over time.
12. **New behaviour:**
    - **The backup command writes its time and its result to Thermite,** and Thermite records a restore it refused. Today Thermite records no backup.
    - **Undo of a removed rule.**

**What waits for another goal**

- Models, Agents, Tools and Access: goal 245. Your account, and tokens made on a screen: goal 261.
- A budget in dollars: goal [123](123-budgets-made-simple.goal), built after this goal.
- A machine's own log: its page in Compute (goal [250](250-rigs-and-machines.goal)); its lines reach control with goal [257](257-find-the-fault.goal).
- The knowledge base's settings: Knowledge (goal [251](251-library.goal)). A run's own cost: its Usage tab (goal 247). A model's price: its provider's page (goal 245).
- More parts on System, once goal [258](258-runs-own-their-resources.goal) makes the control plane several services: each is one more row.

**The five steps,** as for every area ([how a screen is built](../app-build-plan.md#how-a-screen-is-built)):

1. Its mockup, agreed. Done, 2026-11-12.
2. Its reads and actions, in control, with their tests.
3. Its screens, from the app's parts alone.
4. Its cases in the browser check, at three widths, in light and in dark, with the rules' budget: a list for Setup's first screen, Exports and Logs; a detail for Spend, Storage, Backup and System; a form for a rule.
5. Its docs pages, in the same commits.

## Why

- Today's Metrics mixes money with control's internals under one item of the main navigation.
- "What takes space" has 3 pages in 3 areas; the message bus has 5 places.
- The owner, 2026-10-19: the audit log becomes Logs, with audit as one category, and every log of control is visible there.
- A backup is a command and a docs page today: no screen says when the last one was.

## Constraints

- **A mockup first.** Done: Setup's first screen, Spend, Storage, Exports, Backup, Logs, System, and their other states.
- **Names of tables, loops, streams and environment variables show under System alone.**
- **A rule says what it would remove before it is saved,** and never removes a run's record, the project's branches or an export.
- **No caps and no pagers:** the log, the commands and the exports say their whole count and load as they are scrolled.
- **Times are UTC.**

## Done when

- [x] The mockups are approved. Done, 2026-11-12 (goal 243's Decisions).
- [ ] Each read of item 11 is a route of the API with tests there, and the backup command's record has its test.
- [ ] The owner reads 30 days of spend by campaign and by plan, finds an action in Logs by who did it, cancels a command that hangs, makes a rule after reading what it would remove, downloads and deletes an export, and reads when the last backup was, in the app.
- [ ] Setup's first screen says each part's state in one line, and colours the one that is wrong, shown by a test on the demo's data.
- [ ] Goal [027](027-logs-page.goal)'s item, every line control logs in one place with a filter, is done as its open question is answered.
- [ ] Goal [109](109-exports-page-shows-what-matters.goal)'s item, an Exports list that shows what matters, is done as its open question is answered; item 2 of goal 131 is done for an export that is still arriving.
- [ ] The log level of control is set under System (item 6 of goal [178](178-clean-up-continued.goal)).
- [ ] The browser check covers each screen of items 1 to 9, at three widths, in light and in dark, within the rules' budgets.
- [ ] Pages: Spend, the system view, Logs and commands, storage and its rules, exports, backup and restore, and their screenshots.

## Decisions

- 2026-11-10, the owner: accepted into v0.3.0, with the plan of goal [242](_completed/242-v030-review.goal). The dashboard is a web app on fxbot's own stack, and each recommendation of the two guides is taken; where a question is about a look, the recommendation is what is mocked first, and the owner chooses from the mockups.
- 2026-11-12, the owner: the mockup of the whole app and [the app's build plan](../app-build-plan.md) are agreed, and this goal's plan is rewritten to them. What changed here: the area is the rest of Setup, where it was "Usage, Logs and the rest of Settings"; Usage is Spend, under Setup, and a run's own use is the run's Usage tab; Setup opens on one table of its parts, where the plan had Settings in tabs; Exports and Backup are under Storage, and exports came here from goal 251, with goal 109's item; tool servers, the network's addresses and the agents went to goal 245, and the knowledge base's limits to goal 251; the mockup draws a saved rule as on, where this goal's constraint had a policy that removes nothing until the owner turns it on (Open questions).

## Open questions

- Goal [123](123-budgets-made-simple.goal) (one budget in dollars) adds to Spend. It is built after this goal. Which read gives a budget was not checked.
- Where control's own log lines show (goal 027). The mockup's Logs holds who changed what and the commands; of control's own log it has the log level alone, under System.
- Whether a filter by kind is enough for Exports (goal 109). Goal 109 asked that the smaller exports fold under one line; the mockup lists every export, with its kind.
- Whether a rule is on as soon as it is saved. The mockup says so, because the form says what the rule would remove before Save. This goal's constraint of 2026-11-10 said that a policy removes nothing until the owner turns it on. A rule destroys records, so the owner confirms it.
- Whether many exports can be deleted at once. The mockup deletes one at a time.
- Whether the app gets a button that backs up. The mockup shows the command.
- Whether control's read of the system gives each machine's share of what is kept, for Storage's fold.
- Where the log level of a machine's parts is set, with no rig (item 6 of goal 178).

## Progress

- 2026-11-10: Goal written from the review (goal 242).
- 2026-11-10: Accepted by the owner; `READY`.
- 2026-11-12: Rewritten to the agreed mockup and the app's build plan.

